  It's not that characters can't be played differently.  More that 
players *won't* play characters differently in the late game.


  The knight's jumping ability differentiates it at every stage of the
game.  Escape/attack early.  Water crossing in the mid to end-game.
Doubled traveling speed on the Planes of Earth, Fire, and the Astral Plane.
(Imagine if #jumping could be integrated into the travel command on 
non-teleport levels.  I've done it manually on Orcus level.  It's 
impressive.)

  And the Magic Mirror of Merlin doubles the damage done by the magic
missile spell.  XL 30 knight with the MMoM and  (Int > 18) averages
118 points of damage per hit per monster(s), near or far, with the
spell of magic missile.

  There are posts on rgrn going back years about these abilities.

  If you don't play a knight differently from every other class in 
the endgame, that's your fault, not Nethack's.


  I've ascended a full-up XL 30 wizard with the Eye of Aethiopica,
all spells, 0% failure on all spells, and 1000 points of mana.
Any other class is crippled compared to that.  


  Just the divination school: Skilled+ Detect Monster lasts.  Knowing 
where every monster is on the entire level at all times makes Nethack a 
completely different game.  (Especially on the Astral Planes.)

  Add Magic Mapping and Detect Treasure and Gehennom's a breeze.
Identify also has its supporters ;^).  Light is nearly my favorite 
early-game spell.  Clairvoyance isn't blocked on unmappable levels.  

  
  So spell skills alone differentiate classes:

  
